Observe native endpoints and actual recent dispatch on the existing metrics server.
The view refuses pending selection/send windows, unsynchronized membership and
unsupported native profiles. GET does not mutate routing or expire native state.
Removed dispatched listeners retain false selection flags with recent-dispatch evidence.
Observed workers keep conservative circuit_open: false so transient endpoint-health-filter
ejections are never misclassified as permanent retirement.

AGAINST: llm-d/llm-d-router commit 3283d440334109fc785d4380355cc0375fc32755 (post-v1.0.0 main).

Rebased from v1.0.0 onto 3283d440334109fc785d4380355cc0375fc32755:
- PR #3830 merged pkg/epp/framework/interface/requestcontrol into requesthandling.
- PR #3665 added systemone-parser to the default parser set, PR #3328 added
  endpoint-health-filter, parseConfigurationPhaseTwo registers datalayer-poll-status,
  and StaticUsageLimitPolicyType is now "static-usage-limit-policy"; all are registered
  in observer.SupportedPlugins.
- PR #3462 routed WebSocket upgrades through fallbackToEndpoint alongside bodyless GETs;
  fallbackToEndpoint opens the observer window before selecting the fallback endpoint.
- PR #3382 dropped NewCachedEndpointCandidates in favor of NewDatastoreEndpointCandidates,
  and NewDirectorWithConfig gained poolName.
- TestObserverSupportsRenderedOperatorProfiles covers baseline server/pd fixtures plus
  External DP server (omitting prefix-cache-scorer), unmanaged pollFailureThreshold=0,
  precise KV-events PD with dataLayer, and EPD (confirming encode omits
  endpoint-health-filter).

The constructor-based ExtProcServerRunner surfaces every field through
NewExtProcServerRunner, and TestNewExtProcServerRunnerPopulatesEveryField fails
when any new field is zero. Observer is wired by post-constructor assignment in
runner.go and is added to the test's callerSet.

The patch carries the seven datastore observer-revision increments: the
public mutation sites WithEndpointPool, Clear, PoolSet,
PodUpdateOrAddIfNotExist (the exported wrapper), PodDelete,
EndpointUpsert, EndpointDelete. The unexported podUpdateOrAddIfNotExist
helper takes no observerMu acquisition because both its callers
(PodUpdateOrAddIfNotExist and PoolSet via podResyncAll) already increment,
and an observerMu acquisition here would invert the lock order against
ObserverSnapshot (which takes observerMu then ds.mu) into AB-BA deadlock.
pkg/epp/datastore/observer_lock_order_test.go pins this invariant.

The operator collector must consume recent-dispatch evidence before using
this view.

